<section class="page-top section-tight" aria-labelledby="supp-title">
  <div class="wrap page-head wide">
    <h1 id="supp-title">Where supplement brands lose money, and how we handle it.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Built for founder-led supplement brands already selling online. Four problems come with the category. Here is how we handle each one.</p>
    <p>We run systems for two supplement brands today: Mara Labs and Redd Remedies.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/growth-roadmap/" data-cta="supplement_hero_roadmap">Get your Growth Roadmap</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="copy-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-head">
      <h2 id="copy-title">Your ad copy gets scrutinized.</h2>
      <p>Ad platforms review supplement ads closely. One wrong line can get an ad rejected in the middle of a launch.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="body-copy">
      <p class="lede">Copy is checked before it runs.</p>
      <p>Each brand gets a list of what it can and cannot say. Ad copy is checked against that list before it goes live. When you reject a phrase, it is recorded in your brand rules and checked in later drafts.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="sale-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-head">
      <h2 id="sale-title">Sale weeks break in the gaps.</h2>
      <p>A sale lives on the banner, the product page, the landing pages, the cart and the ads. If one of them changes late, buyers see two different deals.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="body-copy">
      <p class="lede">Sales are date-gated across the site and the ads.</p>
      <p>The banner, pages and ads are scheduled to change when the sale starts and when it ends, then checked after the switch. Nobody stays up to do it, and a person works through anything the schedule cannot switch on its own.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="sub-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-head">
      <h2 id="sub-title">Subscriptions carry the math.</h2>
      <p>For a product people reorder, what a buyer is worth depends on the second, third and fourth order, not the first.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="body-copy">
      <p class="lede">The page and the follow-up are built around the repeat order.</p>
      <p>We pre-select subscribe-and-save where the brand agrees, with one-time one tap away. Retention flows keep subscribers hearing from you after the first order. Ads are judged on what a subscriber is worth, not only on the first sale.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="price-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-head">
      <h2 id="price-title">The page says one price. Checkout says another.</h2>
      <p>Bundles, subscription discounts and sale codes stack up. Sooner or later an ad or a landing page promises a price the cart does not honor.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="body-copy">
      <p class="lede">Pages are price-checked against the real cart.</p>
      <p>Before any ad money is spent, the price on the landing page is checked against what checkout charges. One price everywhere.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

